BT /F1 10 Tf 54 626.0 Td (This framework establishes how Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\) governs, maps, measures, and manages) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612.0 Td (risk across the lifecycle of its AI systems. It operationalizes the four core functions of the NIST) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598.0 Td (AI Risk Management Framework \(AI RMF 1.0\) - GOVERN, MAP, MEASURE, and MANAGE - to ensure our AI is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584.0 Td (trustworthy, safe, fair, and accountable. It applies to all HPE-built, HPE-operated, and third-party) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570.0 Td (AI capabilities embedded in our products and internal operations, including GreenLake AIOps, Aruba) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 556.0 Td (AI network insights, HPEFS fraud detection, and Ezmeral ML.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 536.0 Td (Our objective is a repeatable, evidence-based governance program that balances innovation with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 522.0 Td (protection of customers, end users, affected communities, and HPE itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 502.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 476.0 Td (GOVERN - Policy, Accountability, and Oversight) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 453.0 Td (Governance is the foundation on which all other functions rest. HPE maintains an enterprise) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 439.0 Td (Responsible AI Policy that codifies principles of fairness, transparency, safety, privacy, security,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 425.0 Td (and human accountability. The policy is approved by executive leadership and is binding on every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 411.0 Td (business unit that builds or deploys AI.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 391.0 Td (Roles and responsibilities are defined through a formal RACI model and administered by the AI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 377.0 Td (Governance Committee, chaired by the Chief AI Officer and including Legal, Privacy, Security,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 363.0 Td (Product, and business-unit representation. Key accountable roles include:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 343.0 Td (- AI System Owners - accountable for each system's risk posture and compliance \(e.g., the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 329.0 Td (  GreenLake AIOps owner, the HPEFS fraud-detection owner\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 315.0 Td (- Model Stewards / Data Stewards - responsible for data quality, model documentation, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 301.0 Td (  lifecycle records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 287.0 Td (- Responsible AI Office - sets policy, maintains this framework, and provides independent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 273.0 Td (  oversight and assurance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 259.0 Td (- AI Risk & Compliance - validates that risk assessments, controls, and audit evidence are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 245.0 Td (  complete.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 225.0 Td (The Committee sets the enterprise AI risk appetite and risk tolerance, approves high-risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 211.0 Td (deployments, and reviews the risk register quarterly. All governance decisions, approvals, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 197.0 Td (exceptions are logged as auditable evidence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 177.0 Td (An enterprise AI inventory - the AI-BOM and model registry - catalogs every model, its version,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 163.0 Td (training data lineage, intended use, owner, and risk tier. No AI system may enter production unless) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 149.0 Td (it is registered in this catalog and has a named accountable owner.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 129.0 Td (---) Tj ET
